1
00:00:00,075 --> 00:00:04,170
I don’t know anymore whether the victims
or the murderer that’s more of a sicko.

2
00:00:05,481 --> 00:00:09,200
The crime scene Nekros means
for MP Jaratphong must be…

3
00:00:09,290 --> 00:00:10,349
The temple he built.

4
00:00:10,411 --> 00:00:11,402
Hey! Stop!

5
00:00:13,094 --> 00:00:13,742
Phat. Phat.
Phat!

6
00:00:15,229 --> 00:00:18,210
There’s been a speculation
that each victim in this case,

7
00:00:18,362 --> 00:00:22,400
especially MP Jaratphong,
is involved in some shady businesses

8
00:00:22,542 --> 00:00:24,998
and has severely assaulted
the suspect’s family.

9
00:00:25,029 --> 00:00:27,570
Does the police department think
this is a vigilante act that serves

10
00:00:27,684 --> 00:00:30,500
to make up for the delayed justice?

11
00:00:31,488 --> 00:00:33,666
We investigate based on
the witnesses and evidence.

12
00:00:34,388 --> 00:00:37,002
We do not take into consideration
what the backgrounds of the victims are.

13
00:00:37,607 --> 00:00:42,204
Taking someone’s life
is a crime we do not tolerate.

14
00:00:42,940 --> 00:00:45,198
We will let the laws decide
what is right or wrong.

15
00:00:49,780 --> 00:00:55,450
Are you talking about the same laws
that failed to protect Kim’s family

16
00:00:55,697 --> 00:00:59,503
and caused an innocent child
to grow up to be a murderer?

17
00:01:05,521 --> 00:01:10,109
How can you be certain, sir,
that you can really give him justice,

18
00:01:10,850 --> 00:01:18,000
instead of just silencing someone
who’s wrong to save his humanity?

19
00:01:20,066 --> 00:01:22,903
Our job is to enforce the laws
that keep our society in check.

20
00:01:24,280 --> 00:01:25,770
Bringing up the past

21
00:01:25,804 --> 00:01:28,550
might be a little too complicated
to bring up right now.

22
00:01:29,816 --> 00:01:31,401
Thank you all for your attention.

23
00:01:32,897 --> 00:01:33,665
Sir.

24
00:01:33,703 --> 00:01:35,057
Sir, please answer the questions.

25
00:01:36,220 --> 00:01:36,942
Sir.
Sir.

26
00:01:37,891 --> 00:01:38,850
-Sir.
-Sir.

27
00:03:02,665 --> 00:03:03,400
Praew.

28
00:03:06,625 --> 00:03:09,802
He woke up to eat
and just fell back asleep.

29
00:03:11,602 --> 00:03:13,663
Oh, Kaye. I have something to tell you.

30
00:03:14,131 --> 00:03:17,903
Phat opened his eyes
and didn’t even ask about me one bit.

31
00:03:18,222 --> 00:03:19,201
He asked about you.

32
00:03:19,659 --> 00:03:20,801
Should I be offended?

33
00:03:25,413 --> 00:03:26,200
Bye.

34
00:03:59,152 --> 00:04:00,302
What are you doing out there?

35
00:04:01,948 --> 00:04:03,903
What are you getting up for?

36
00:04:13,345 --> 00:04:15,700
Is your wound good enough
to be walking around like this?

37
00:04:33,370 --> 00:04:36,699
Who’d have thought my first days off
would be a long holiday?

38
00:04:40,940 --> 00:04:42,099
Thank you…

39
00:04:43,382 --> 00:04:45,497
for risking your life to save me.

40
00:04:50,108 --> 00:04:51,659
Why are you thanking me?

41
00:04:53,480 --> 00:04:56,248
It was my job as a cop anyway.

42
00:04:59,008 --> 00:05:02,896
At least now you know
there are still some good cops out there.

43
00:05:14,737 --> 00:05:15,902
It’s been a long time…

44
00:05:17,668 --> 00:05:20,300
since I could let my mind
be at peace like this.

45
00:05:23,026 --> 00:05:25,905
Was your previous case just as rough?

46
00:05:29,490 --> 00:05:31,902
This case is… the worst so far.

47
00:05:42,450 --> 00:05:43,502
Honestly…

48
00:05:44,663 --> 00:05:45,496
You…

49
00:05:47,230 --> 00:05:49,148
You didn’t need to save someone like me.

50
00:05:51,462 --> 00:05:54,149
You should have let me pay for what I did

51
00:05:55,080 --> 00:05:56,699
and let me mess it up completely.

52
00:06:03,740 --> 00:06:04,997
If you were gonna mess it up,

53
00:06:07,540 --> 00:06:11,654
I’d love to help you
before you ruin the entire thing.

54
00:06:32,880 --> 00:06:34,700
(It’s been three days)

55
00:06:34,832 --> 00:06:40,398
(since the police took the suspect behind
the Nekros serial murder into custody)

56
00:06:40,528 --> 00:06:44,497
(after tireless investigation
and intense cooperation.)

57
00:06:44,896 --> 00:06:51,565
(We’ll see what is waiting at the end
of the tunnel for this vigilante.)

58
00:06:51,660 --> 00:06:55,352
(This case has tremendously uplifted
the image of the police department)

59
00:06:55,385 --> 00:06:57,660
(which has been subpar for so long.)

60
00:06:57,790 --> 00:07:01,100
(The public is surely
keeping their eyes on this case.)

61
00:07:04,851 --> 00:07:06,410
Your wound’s not completely healed.

62
00:07:06,586 --> 00:07:08,100
Why are you bringing yourself to work?

63
00:07:10,872 --> 00:07:12,002
Worried about me?

64
00:07:16,720 --> 00:07:18,103
I need to get this case closed.

65
00:07:18,786 --> 00:07:19,920
I can’t waste any time.

66
00:07:20,739 --> 00:07:22,702
The press is putting us
under a lot of pressure.

67
00:07:23,410 --> 00:07:24,699
If I let it go on any longer,

68
00:07:24,950 --> 00:07:27,130
it would just cause
a collective anxiety in the public.

69
00:07:28,250 --> 00:07:29,050
What about you?

70
00:07:29,331 --> 00:07:32,602
Are you sure you want to see
that sicko investigated?

71
00:07:33,628 --> 00:07:34,497
Of course.

72
00:07:35,228 --> 00:07:36,795
I think I might be useful.

73
00:07:37,712 --> 00:07:39,100
Alright. Let’s go.

74
00:07:56,294 --> 00:07:58,096
Surprise!

75
00:07:59,222 --> 00:08:00,770
Welcome back to work, Inspector.

76
00:08:00,933 --> 00:08:04,244
We were nearly killed closing this case.
Weren’t we, guys?

77
00:08:09,235 --> 00:08:10,401
Thank you.

78
00:08:11,134 --> 00:08:12,103
Well done, all of you.

79
00:08:12,488 --> 00:08:15,305
But if you’re done celebrating, tidy up.

80
00:08:15,539 --> 00:08:16,410
Our work isn’t over.

81
00:08:16,668 --> 00:08:17,896
Ugh!

82
00:08:18,285 --> 00:08:20,198
Go on. Get back to work.

83
00:08:20,992 --> 00:08:24,598
Get ready to question Kim
so we can get on with his confession.

84
00:08:24,946 --> 00:08:26,000
More importantly,

85
00:08:26,485 --> 00:08:28,290
we need to send this to the prosecutor
as soon as possible

86
00:08:28,438 --> 00:08:30,800
before the press makes even more
of a mess of this case.

87
00:08:31,050 --> 00:08:32,299
-Yes, sir.
-Yes, sir.

88
00:08:33,610 --> 00:08:34,400
Inspector.

89
00:08:35,440 --> 00:08:36,871
Don’t worry about the report.

90
00:08:37,121 --> 00:08:38,930
Our crime lab just sent in the results,

91
00:08:39,108 --> 00:08:42,530
and Kim’s DNA and fingerprints
are all over all the crime scenes.

92
00:08:44,470 --> 00:08:47,002
With this kind of evidence,
there’s no way he’s getting away.

93
00:08:47,650 --> 00:08:48,499
Good work, Nop.

94
00:08:48,668 --> 00:08:49,480
Yes, sir.

95
00:08:59,727 --> 00:09:01,499
(Who is Anan Pratonngam or Kim,)

96
00:09:01,750 --> 00:09:03,660
(the serial murderer
behind the Nekros murders)

97
00:09:03,682 --> 00:09:05,660
(who has just been arrested?)

98
00:09:06,380 --> 00:09:08,628
(Let me take you back in time.)

99
00:09:09,454 --> 00:09:13,660
(Little Kim was crying for justice.)

100
00:09:14,140 --> 00:09:16,798
(He was the only witness)

101
00:09:17,318 --> 00:09:20,330
(when his mother was brutally murdered
and ransacked for her organs.)

102
00:09:20,850 --> 00:09:23,662
(This human trafficking business
was clearcut)

103
00:09:23,927 --> 00:09:26,240
(and directly
involved with MP Jaratphong.)

104
00:09:26,574 --> 00:09:28,130
(But no matter
how obvious the business was,)

105
00:09:28,334 --> 00:09:30,102
(this case still went silent.)

106
00:09:30,668 --> 00:09:33,300
(Kim became a homeless orphan,)

107
00:09:33,890 --> 00:09:38,102
(watching the famous MP
enjoying his time in the spotlight.)

108
00:09:38,928 --> 00:09:40,699
(It raises the question:)

109
00:09:41,385 --> 00:09:48,640
(Is Kim a vicious devil or a victim
of the miscarriage of justice?)

110
00:10:19,830 --> 00:10:21,801
You’re thinking his life is miserable.

111
00:10:29,010 --> 00:10:32,497
That is no excuse to take anyone’s life.

112
00:10:35,242 --> 00:10:40,502
Maybe he just needs his voice to be heard.

113
00:10:41,007 --> 00:10:44,900
And that’s why we need to go
and listen to him with our own ears.

114
00:10:49,743 --> 00:10:50,602
You ready?

115
00:10:52,260 --> 00:10:53,951
I’m going to investigate him now.

116
00:11:13,642 --> 00:11:15,299
I thought you were dead!

117
00:11:18,345 --> 00:11:19,903
(Congrats, sir.)

118
00:11:20,650 --> 00:11:22,100
(What a relief you made it through
so we could have a chat.)

119
00:11:22,493 --> 00:11:23,657
How is your wound?

120
00:11:25,860 --> 00:11:26,700
Nosy bastard.

121
00:11:30,970 --> 00:11:31,899
But well…

122
00:11:32,952 --> 00:11:35,097
You came all this way to see me.

123
00:11:36,411 --> 00:11:38,102
What business, sir?

124
00:11:38,739 --> 00:11:40,700
Just say what you need to say.

125
00:11:42,420 --> 00:11:44,497
Whether or not you confess,

126
00:11:45,699 --> 00:11:46,802
in the end,

127
00:11:48,709 --> 00:11:50,995
you will surrender
in front of the evidence.

128
00:11:54,850 --> 00:11:56,502
How about this, Inspector?

129
00:11:57,259 --> 00:11:58,702
I’ll tell you a story.

130
00:12:00,648 --> 00:12:02,330
You remember that pig?

131
00:12:04,087 --> 00:12:07,210
When I plunged the knife into his skin

132
00:12:08,970 --> 00:12:11,204
and slowly dragged it…

133
00:12:12,453 --> 00:12:13,300
Whoosh!

134
00:12:15,792 --> 00:12:17,402
I took my time filleting him.

135
00:12:19,318 --> 00:12:22,899
Filleting his flabby skin

136
00:12:23,660 --> 00:12:24,946
and threw it in the toilet.

137
00:12:27,161 --> 00:12:28,398
And his voice, sir…

138
00:12:29,269 --> 00:12:33,100
He was wailing like pigs
in a slaughterhouse.

139
00:12:34,840 --> 00:12:35,998
Listen up, sir.

140
00:12:36,510 --> 00:12:40,303
If I listen very closely right now,
I can still hear his voice ringing in my ears.

141
00:12:47,995 --> 00:12:50,500
(Do you think Mr. Kill
would be proud of me, Inspector?)

142
00:12:53,448 --> 00:12:56,400
I did everything exactly like in the manga.

143
00:12:57,078 --> 00:13:00,994
I took the knife
and made an upside down pentagram.

144
00:13:02,097 --> 00:13:03,297
(That’s not all, sir.)

145
00:13:03,447 --> 00:13:05,102
Before I bashed his head open,

146
00:13:05,371 --> 00:13:08,899
I was meticulous in comparing it
to the panels in the manga.

147
00:13:09,337 --> 00:13:10,500
Making sure it’s perfect.

148
00:13:10,630 --> 00:13:12,920
I was aiming and then I smashed!

149
00:13:15,520 --> 00:13:17,657
With the first blow,
his head went like this.

150
00:13:18,798 --> 00:13:19,610
But he didn’t bleed.

151
00:13:21,198 --> 00:13:23,600
So I smashed again, sir!

152
00:13:24,164 --> 00:13:27,002
And that did the job, Inspector.

153
00:13:28,223 --> 00:13:30,102
He was bleeding like…

154
00:13:30,668 --> 00:13:31,500
Hmm.

155
00:13:31,860 --> 00:13:32,697
Kim.

156
00:13:35,140 --> 00:13:36,300
I’ll tell you what.

157
00:13:38,616 --> 00:13:40,697
No one is proud of you.

158
00:13:43,656 --> 00:13:44,400
Oh.

159
00:13:45,887 --> 00:13:46,802
One more thing…

160
00:13:48,635 --> 00:13:50,102
Your beloved prophet?

161
00:13:51,475 --> 00:13:54,099
He’s so disappointed in you.

162
00:13:55,471 --> 00:13:58,050
Because your work sucks so damn bad.

163
00:13:58,122 --> 00:13:59,394
How could he be disappointed?

164
00:13:59,800 --> 00:14:02,296
(How dare you say that to me,
you jerkass Inspector!)

165
00:14:02,700 --> 00:14:06,102
It’s because of cops like you
that the world needs Nekros.

166
00:14:07,760 --> 00:14:09,300
That’s not true. It can’t be true!

167
00:14:09,885 --> 00:14:11,660
Mr. Kill must be proud of me.

168
00:14:12,010 --> 00:14:13,404
I made sure to get all the details.

169
00:14:15,290 --> 00:14:16,402
Go away, you asshole!

170
00:14:16,714 --> 00:14:18,402
Shut your dirty hole, freaking cop.

171
00:14:20,260 --> 00:14:21,401
He doesn’t know anything.

172
00:14:21,570 --> 00:14:23,299
Cops like him don’t know shit.

173
00:14:24,830 --> 00:14:26,401
I suggest you keep your mouth shut

174
00:14:28,708 --> 00:14:31,400
since you’ll have plenty of time
to talk in prison, Kim.

175
00:14:32,742 --> 00:14:33,659
Go away!

176
00:14:34,214 --> 00:14:35,400
It can’t be true!

177
00:14:35,800 --> 00:14:37,500
You don’t know Mr. Kill as well as I do.

178
00:14:37,663 --> 00:14:38,601
(No way!)

179
00:14:38,908 --> 00:14:39,748
(It’s not true.)

180
00:14:39,773 --> 00:14:40,890
(He was just talking nonsense.)

181
00:14:41,179 --> 00:14:42,100
(It’s not true.)

182
00:14:43,788 --> 00:14:45,001
(He was just threatening me.)

183
00:14:48,189 --> 00:14:49,000
Right?

184
00:14:49,870 --> 00:14:50,899
I see you through!

185
00:14:51,515 --> 00:14:52,700
(That was just a threat.)

186
00:14:53,081 --> 00:14:54,002
(I know it.)

187
00:15:20,674 --> 00:15:21,662
Let’s go home.

188
00:15:22,115 --> 00:15:23,200
You’ve been staring at Kim so much

189
00:15:23,220 --> 00:15:25,004
his face might as well
jump out of the screen.

190
00:15:25,750 --> 00:15:29,002
I can’t listen to my parents complain
about my late nights anymore, you know?

191
00:15:29,690 --> 00:15:32,502
You don’t think this is too easy?

192
00:15:33,324 --> 00:15:34,899
Everything seems too perfectly staged.

193
00:15:37,920 --> 00:15:41,397
If you think something’s wrong,
then I guess it is.

194
00:15:44,054 --> 00:15:45,697
Oh, it’s my mom.

195
00:15:46,105 --> 00:15:47,610
I need to go.

196
00:15:48,251 --> 00:15:49,561
I’ll be here early tomorrow to help you.

197
00:15:50,100 --> 00:15:51,103
-See you.
-Get home safe.

198
00:15:51,605 --> 00:15:52,500
Bye.

199
00:15:58,690 --> 00:16:00,299
Oh, you’re still here.

200
00:16:02,367 --> 00:16:03,711
I’m just looking through something.

201
00:16:03,733 --> 00:16:04,700
I’ll go home soon.

202
00:16:06,842 --> 00:16:08,097
Oh, Praew.

203
00:16:08,740 --> 00:16:10,703
Do you know who this person is?

204
00:16:11,474 --> 00:16:14,299
I saw him sticking
to your big brother’s side the whole time.

205
00:16:23,087 --> 00:16:24,002
Okay.

206
00:16:24,470 --> 00:16:26,401
If you’re not comfortable telling me,
it’s alright.

207
00:16:27,087 --> 00:16:30,201
Let’s say you just need to say yes or no.

208
00:16:31,976 --> 00:16:32,899
Alright?

209
00:16:34,870 --> 00:16:35,598
Yes.

210
00:16:36,734 --> 00:16:42,100
I’ve been wondering why your brother…

211
00:16:42,899 --> 00:16:47,198
has a romance manga artist
like K.Cupid as his consultant.

212
00:16:48,943 --> 00:16:50,499
But I was at my wit’s end,

213
00:16:51,474 --> 00:16:54,897
unless Kaye is Mr. Kill.

214
00:17:00,865 --> 00:17:01,657
Am I right?

215
00:17:10,583 --> 00:17:15,040
I guess it’s time Mr. Kill makes
his identity public to his fans.

216
00:17:26,631 --> 00:17:28,002
No need to hold back, guys.

217
00:17:28,201 --> 00:17:29,398
This is my mother’s restaurant.

218
00:17:29,770 --> 00:17:31,004
We can stay till sunrise!

219
00:17:31,041 --> 00:17:32,056
Alright!

220
00:17:35,859 --> 00:17:37,659
Mom, come on.

221
00:17:38,510 --> 00:17:40,762
It’s not every day
we get to celebrate like this.

222
00:17:40,780 --> 00:17:41,602
Am I right?

223
00:17:41,914 --> 00:17:43,170
Inspector is here, Mom.

224
00:17:43,328 --> 00:17:44,195
Mwah, mwah.

225
00:17:45,714 --> 00:17:47,657
Look at how beautiful she is, guys.

226
00:17:47,970 --> 00:17:49,302
Oh, my sweet talker.

227
00:17:49,600 --> 00:17:50,620
Go on and sit down.

228
00:17:51,660 --> 00:17:53,065
You can all make yourselves at home.

229
00:17:53,097 --> 00:17:55,200
If you need anything,
please just let Nop know.

230
00:17:55,235 --> 00:17:57,088
-Thank you, ma’am.
-Thank you.

231
00:17:57,111 --> 00:17:58,278
Have a great time.

232
00:17:58,404 --> 00:17:59,660
Love you, Mom.

233
00:18:00,050 --> 00:18:02,000
Oh, look at you.

234
00:18:02,026 --> 00:18:05,050
You still coddle up to your mama
at this big age?

235
00:18:05,339 --> 00:18:07,598
You don’t look the type!

236
00:18:08,385 --> 00:18:09,802
Don’t make fun of me.

237
00:18:13,555 --> 00:18:16,460
Mr. Chaiwat asks me
to give you this bottle of wine

238
00:18:16,481 --> 00:18:19,659
to celebrate your closing a national case.

239
00:18:20,478 --> 00:18:23,097
I bet you’ll be my boss
within a few years.

240
00:18:24,068 --> 00:18:25,671
I’ll be in your care.

241
00:18:26,940 --> 00:18:29,810
Give my thanks to Uncle Chaiwat.

242
00:18:32,991 --> 00:18:35,659
Inspector, please have a seat.

243
00:18:35,700 --> 00:18:37,896
This is my mother’s restaurant.
I’ll take care of you.

244
00:18:38,026 --> 00:18:39,001
What do you drink?

245
00:18:39,062 --> 00:18:40,096
Wine or beer?

246
00:18:42,823 --> 00:18:43,662
Anything is fine by me.

247
00:18:44,297 --> 00:18:45,210
Alright. Please have a seat.

248
00:18:45,234 --> 00:18:46,402
You must be hungry.

249
00:18:47,755 --> 00:18:48,598
Alright, guys.

250
00:18:48,690 --> 00:18:49,665
Make room.

251
00:18:53,030 --> 00:18:53,840
Here you go.

252
00:18:54,522 --> 00:18:55,299
Here.

253
00:18:55,416 --> 00:18:56,900
Aren’t you hungry?

254
00:18:57,920 --> 00:18:59,102
I can’t really stomach anything.

255
00:18:59,429 --> 00:19:00,299
But thank you.

256
00:19:05,899 --> 00:19:06,801
Here.

257
00:19:07,536 --> 00:19:09,400
The biggest piece for our MVP.

258
00:19:10,819 --> 00:19:11,598
Thank you.

259
00:19:12,050 --> 00:19:15,502
Without Kaye,
we wouldn’t be able to close this case.

260
00:19:15,980 --> 00:19:17,659
You were a big help. Thank you.

261
00:19:18,185 --> 00:19:20,700
Guys, let’s raise our cups for Kaye!

262
00:19:21,096 --> 00:19:22,097
Bottoms up!

263
00:19:22,444 --> 00:19:23,302
Alright.

264
00:19:23,592 --> 00:19:24,060
Come on.

265
00:19:24,090 --> 00:19:25,500
In three, two, one…

266
00:19:25,607 --> 00:19:27,654
Cheers!

267
00:19:32,210 --> 00:19:33,200
Drink up, y’all.

268
00:19:42,075 --> 00:19:44,170
Why did you sneak out
to make that serious face?

269
00:19:47,613 --> 00:19:48,503
What?

270
00:19:49,260 --> 00:19:50,648
I just needed some fresh air.

271
00:19:51,165 --> 00:19:52,103
I was just thinking.

272
00:20:00,068 --> 00:20:00,871
You want a puff?

273
00:20:02,410 --> 00:20:03,200
Thank you.

274
00:20:10,311 --> 00:20:11,660
Work’s done.

275
00:20:12,296 --> 00:20:13,660
Case closed.

276
00:20:15,250 --> 00:20:17,500
Can you stop making a face like

277
00:20:17,760 --> 00:20:19,503
you’re thinking about
having someone arrested?

278
00:20:24,265 --> 00:20:26,598
See? You actually know how to smile.

279
00:20:27,540 --> 00:20:28,840
Because if you don’t,

280
00:20:29,480 --> 00:20:31,195
I’ll start getting stressed out, too.

281
00:20:45,348 --> 00:20:46,300
Here they come!

282
00:20:51,776 --> 00:20:53,660
Mr. Kim, how are you feeling?

283
00:20:54,071 --> 00:20:55,234
Anything to say to the people?

284
00:20:55,260 --> 00:20:56,330
Who hired you?

285
00:20:56,626 --> 00:20:57,770
What was your motivation?

286
00:20:57,945 --> 00:20:59,802
Why did you choose to imitate Nekros?

287
00:20:59,888 --> 00:21:01,397
What is your association with the victims?

288
00:21:25,657 --> 00:21:26,390
Stay still!
Kim!

289
00:21:30,570 --> 00:21:32,730
How does it feel to be praised
for doing something wrong?

290
00:21:33,102 --> 00:21:34,990
What do you think of the fact
people think you’re a hero?

291
00:21:35,010 --> 00:21:35,949
Who hired you?

292
00:21:35,970 --> 00:21:37,398
Do you accept your judgement?

293
00:21:38,114 --> 00:21:39,700
Do you believe justice will be served?

294
00:21:40,117 --> 00:21:41,100
Give us an answer.

295
00:21:44,634 --> 00:21:46,602
It is stuffy inside, isn’t it?

296
00:21:48,712 --> 00:21:49,602
Well…

297
00:21:50,240 --> 00:21:52,201
I have a question.

298
00:21:52,943 --> 00:21:54,800
If Kim wasn’t arrested right now,

299
00:21:55,660 --> 00:21:57,299
who would be the next victim?

300
00:22:00,817 --> 00:22:02,602
Oh, my name is Thun.

301
00:22:02,970 --> 00:22:05,499
Should I call you Kaye…

302
00:22:07,180 --> 00:22:08,497
or Mr. Kill?

303
00:22:12,480 --> 00:22:13,299
Uh…

304
00:22:13,472 --> 00:22:15,103
What do you want?

305
00:22:15,509 --> 00:22:21,201
I just want a short interview with you
as the artist who created Nekros.

306
00:22:26,004 --> 00:22:26,727
I’m sorry.

307
00:22:26,755 --> 00:22:28,250
I’m not available for interviews.

308
00:22:28,527 --> 00:22:29,324
Excuse me.

309
00:22:29,351 --> 00:22:30,402
Mr. Kaye.

310
00:22:31,327 --> 00:22:33,398
If you choose to stay silent,

311
00:22:34,277 --> 00:22:36,699
lies will become truths.

312
00:22:37,920 --> 00:22:40,000
Because the person
who knows the truth like you

313
00:22:40,680 --> 00:22:42,201
chooses to stay silent.

314
00:22:52,900 --> 00:22:56,210
Don’t forget
what your father went through,

315
00:22:57,814 --> 00:23:01,657
and who destroyed your family.

316
00:23:06,600 --> 00:23:07,660
Remember.

317
00:23:08,960 --> 00:23:13,002
What did you have to do
when you created the demon like Nekros?

318
00:23:17,400 --> 00:23:18,896
Hey. What are you doing?

319
00:23:25,293 --> 00:23:27,001
I’m not doing anything wrong, sir.

320
00:23:27,677 --> 00:23:29,000
I’m only speaking the truth.

321
00:23:30,308 --> 00:23:34,899
Or is it wrong in this country
to tell the truth?

322
00:23:37,110 --> 00:23:39,048
And there are so many things…

323
00:23:39,808 --> 00:23:43,899
Kaye doesn’t know, such as…

324
00:23:45,080 --> 00:23:46,700
Your father.

325
00:23:54,760 --> 00:23:56,201
You wanna be on my nerves, huh?

326
00:23:56,440 --> 00:23:58,065
I’m done putting up with it, you jerk!

327
00:23:58,957 --> 00:24:00,059
Make way!

328
00:24:00,798 --> 00:24:01,518
Phat!

329
00:24:02,140 --> 00:24:02,875
you jerk!

330
00:24:03,072 --> 00:24:04,000
Phat, stop!

331
00:24:06,075 --> 00:24:06,899
Inspector!

332
00:24:07,930 --> 00:24:08,648
Stop it!

333
00:24:23,998 --> 00:24:26,001
Do you realize what you just did?

334
00:24:29,880 --> 00:24:32,200
I know I was wrong.

335
00:24:34,651 --> 00:24:39,503
Your job is to enforce laws,
not being a bully.

336
00:24:40,512 --> 00:24:42,503
And the first thing you need

337
00:24:42,847 --> 00:24:44,902
to learn how to do is
how to control your emotions.

338
00:24:45,549 --> 00:24:48,900
Don’t allow anyone to use them
against you like this.

339
00:24:52,211 --> 00:24:53,302
I’m sorry, Uncle.

340
00:24:54,589 --> 00:24:58,299
I promise it won’t happen again.

341
00:25:07,610 --> 00:25:09,897
I got an order of suspension for you,

342
00:25:11,863 --> 00:25:14,500
as well as an order to set up a committee
to investigate your behavior.

343
00:25:14,960 --> 00:25:16,696
The effect is immediate.

344
00:25:26,280 --> 00:25:27,903
I tried to help you, Phat.

345
00:25:29,180 --> 00:25:31,330
But the video of you punching
that reporter is all over the internet.

346
00:25:34,565 --> 00:25:36,000
I really can’t protect you.

347
00:26:02,722 --> 00:26:03,802
Oh, Inspector?

348
00:26:07,248 --> 00:26:08,299
How’s your hand?

349
00:26:09,653 --> 00:26:11,699
It’s… alright.

350
00:26:13,214 --> 00:26:14,130
Dinner?

351
00:26:16,065 --> 00:26:17,401
Do you want to have dinner with me?

352
00:26:18,250 --> 00:26:19,570
I’ll wait downstairs.

353
00:26:28,074 --> 00:26:30,303
Well, you’re suspended.

354
00:26:30,856 --> 00:26:31,902
Are you alright?

355
00:26:33,470 --> 00:26:34,601
I’m okay.

356
00:26:36,327 --> 00:26:38,197
I haven’t had time to rest at all before.

357
00:26:38,960 --> 00:26:41,297
But now that I closed the case,
it feels like a holiday to me.

358
00:26:44,051 --> 00:26:47,201
Don’t you have anywhere you want to go
during your break, then?

359
00:26:48,465 --> 00:26:49,401
You have time?

360
00:26:51,614 --> 00:26:52,404
Why?

361
00:26:54,640 --> 00:26:55,600
Hmm…

362
00:26:57,210 --> 00:26:58,299
Come with me.

363
00:27:03,367 --> 00:27:04,294
Alright. Kick.

364
00:27:20,110 --> 00:27:21,045
It’s for your own good.

365
00:27:21,850 --> 00:27:23,725
You might run into
those debt collectors again.

366
00:27:23,770 --> 00:27:25,302
At least you’ll be able to put up a fight.

367
00:27:26,577 --> 00:27:27,404
Ready?

368
00:27:27,828 --> 00:27:28,600
Huh?

369
00:27:30,500 --> 00:27:31,897
If you’re not ready, this is what you get.

370
00:27:33,951 --> 00:27:35,597
Oh, wow, Inspector.

371
00:27:36,430 --> 00:27:37,995
Is your injury all healed up now?

372
00:27:38,420 --> 00:27:40,097
Maybe. It’s just a throb.

373
00:27:41,272 --> 00:27:42,004
Come on.

374
00:27:58,940 --> 00:27:59,970
Pick up the gun.

375
00:28:01,699 --> 00:28:02,401
Like this?
Yeah.

376
00:28:04,823 --> 00:28:06,000
Keep your arms straight.

377
00:28:08,000 --> 00:28:08,998
Bend forward a little.

378
00:28:10,170 --> 00:28:12,351
Make sure the middle
of the gun is straight.

379
00:28:14,422 --> 00:28:15,657
Alright. Straight.

380
00:28:16,965 --> 00:28:18,204
Put your finger on the trigger.

381
00:28:18,330 --> 00:28:19,102
Okay.

382
00:28:19,370 --> 00:28:20,097
Yeah.

383
00:28:25,520 --> 00:28:26,650
Pull the trigger.

384
00:28:39,591 --> 00:28:40,645
See?

385
00:28:40,820 --> 00:28:42,201
Told you it’s easy.

386
00:28:47,840 --> 00:28:48,666
Yeah.

387
00:29:12,407 --> 00:29:13,500
Your lighter’s no good.

388
00:29:25,497 --> 00:29:26,274
Thanks.

389
00:29:31,493 --> 00:29:32,900
What does sensei mean?

390
00:29:34,360 --> 00:29:36,700
It’s Japanese.

391
00:29:37,543 --> 00:29:38,502
It means ‘teacher.’

392
00:29:39,816 --> 00:29:40,490
Why?

393
00:29:41,770 --> 00:29:43,699
Praew texted me.

394
00:29:44,737 --> 00:29:46,197
I told her I’m with you.

395
00:29:46,832 --> 00:29:49,680
She said, “Say hello to sensei for me.”

396
00:29:53,350 --> 00:29:54,099
Oh.

397
00:29:54,362 --> 00:29:55,297
Well…

398
00:29:56,183 --> 00:29:57,697
Say hello to her for me.

399
00:29:58,240 --> 00:29:58,997
Sure.

400
00:30:02,740 --> 00:30:03,598
Oh, and…

401
00:30:04,379 --> 00:30:05,949
When are you going back to work?

402
00:30:08,139 --> 00:30:10,000
I have an interview on Monday.

403
00:30:12,550 --> 00:30:14,200
I think I might be suspended for a week…

404
00:30:15,200 --> 00:30:16,328
or a month.

405
00:30:20,530 --> 00:30:21,397
I…

406
00:30:22,240 --> 00:30:23,201
I’m sorry.

407
00:30:24,752 --> 00:30:25,995
Stop apologizing.

408
00:30:27,837 --> 00:30:29,201
It’s not your fault.

409
00:30:31,320 --> 00:30:32,500
And honestly…

410
00:30:33,630 --> 00:30:35,204
He had it coming.

411
00:30:37,445 --> 00:30:38,802
If you think about it,

412
00:30:39,510 --> 00:30:43,100
he was trying to pit me and my sister
against each other.

413
00:30:45,030 --> 00:30:46,598
He deserved that.

414
00:30:49,550 --> 00:30:51,900
Oh, and if you wonder if I’m sorry…

415
00:30:53,370 --> 00:30:54,302
I’m not.

416
00:31:08,497 --> 00:31:09,303
Phat.

417
00:31:09,990 --> 00:31:10,802
Hmm?

418
00:31:12,714 --> 00:31:14,351
Do you think Nekros…

419
00:31:16,490 --> 00:31:17,902
really is Kim?

420
00:31:22,813 --> 00:31:27,210
Us police officers don’t get to decide
based on our gut feelings.

421
00:31:29,217 --> 00:31:31,102
Kim confessed.

422
00:31:32,272 --> 00:31:36,402
And all the evidence
pointed to him as Nekros.

423
00:31:43,776 --> 00:31:44,502
Kaye.

424
00:31:45,217 --> 00:31:46,000
Hmm?

425
00:31:46,502 --> 00:31:49,902
Everything's over now.

426
00:31:51,760 --> 00:31:55,402
You need to move on as well.

427
00:31:57,100 --> 00:31:59,300
And don’t look back.

428
00:32:01,410 --> 00:32:02,296
Sure thing.

429
00:32:02,810 --> 00:32:04,660
I don’t plan to write
any more chapters for Nekros.

430
00:33:29,840 --> 00:33:32,570
MAILBOX (NO TITLE)

431
00:33:37,200 --> 00:33:38,330
CONTACT ME BACK.

432
00:33:39,600 --> 00:33:42,090
CONTACT ME BACK. FROM MR. KILL.

433
00:33:43,400 --> 00:33:45,370
SEND

434
00:33:50,780 --> 00:33:52,699
I ruined everything at the end, Prim.

435
00:33:52,877 --> 00:33:54,050
(Come on.)

436
00:33:54,460 --> 00:33:57,410
(Even if you didn’t tell him,
Thun would have found out anyway.)

437
00:33:57,768 --> 00:33:59,201
(What we need to focus on right now)

438
00:33:59,269 --> 00:34:01,903
(is the scoop for Kim
we’ve been assigned.)

439
00:34:03,586 --> 00:34:06,000
(I heard Thun tell the team today)

440
00:34:06,037 --> 00:34:10,303
(that Kim doesn’t let
his relatives or reporters in.)

441
00:34:11,134 --> 00:34:12,850
(So it’s hopeless
to get an interview with him.)

442
00:34:24,520 --> 00:34:26,597
Prim, I think there’s still hope.

443
00:34:27,570 --> 00:34:28,368
I have to go.
Bye.

444
00:34:29,570 --> 00:34:30,300
(Bye.)

445
00:34:30,920 --> 00:34:31,800
Hello.

446
00:34:32,271 --> 00:34:33,397
(Hello, Praew.)

447
00:34:33,841 --> 00:34:35,570
Sorry to bother you so late.

448
00:34:35,958 --> 00:34:36,801
(Did you…)

449
00:34:37,508 --> 00:34:42,010
Did you know I got all the information
for Nekros from my fans on my blog?

450
00:34:42,797 --> 00:34:45,610
Is that why there’s a tiny watermark
of the username on the cover?

451
00:34:46,140 --> 00:34:46,900
Yes.

452
00:34:49,471 --> 00:34:51,299
I found something strange.

453
00:34:52,440 --> 00:34:54,902
Every chapter of Nekros
that the crimes were based on…

454
00:34:55,520 --> 00:34:57,197
is from the same user.

455
00:34:57,762 --> 00:34:58,700
The name is…

456
00:35:00,265 --> 00:35:01,198
Asura.

457
00:35:04,085 --> 00:35:06,730
I’ve been trying to contact Asura.

458
00:35:07,663 --> 00:35:09,100
But there’s no answer.

459
00:35:09,620 --> 00:35:11,051
Now I want to know…

460
00:35:12,047 --> 00:35:15,900
if there’s any more chapters of Nekros
with Asura’s contribution.

461
00:35:16,056 --> 00:35:18,800
You want to find
the missing Nekros files, is that it?

462
00:35:19,011 --> 00:35:19,780
(Yes.)
I’ll help you.

463
00:35:20,851 --> 00:35:21,728
Thank you.

464
00:35:21,761 --> 00:35:22,800
It’s alright.

465
00:35:23,425 --> 00:35:25,299
I need a favor as well.

466
00:35:27,946 --> 00:35:28,804
What is it?

467
00:35:31,351 --> 00:35:33,100
Don’t worry about Asura.

468
00:35:33,520 --> 00:35:36,497
I posted something in the Nekros fan blog.

469
00:35:36,614 --> 00:35:40,299
I’m sure someone has those old files.

470
00:35:41,241 --> 00:35:42,595
I’ll hurry home and check.

471
00:35:44,668 --> 00:35:47,520
Honestly I’m not worried about that.

472
00:35:48,030 --> 00:35:51,797
I’m more worried about
what we’re doing right now.

473
00:35:53,030 --> 00:35:56,004
If Phat finds out,
he’s going to be so mad at us.

474
00:35:59,730 --> 00:36:01,051
Are you Mr. Chankacha?

475
00:36:01,617 --> 00:36:02,401
Yes.

476
00:36:02,823 --> 00:36:06,497
The inmate agrees to see
you and your friend.

477
00:36:07,671 --> 00:36:08,499
Please come in.

478
00:36:24,474 --> 00:36:26,600
I’m really happy you came to see me.

479
00:36:27,490 --> 00:36:30,810
I want to ask you about
your motivations for murders—

480
00:36:32,727 --> 00:36:33,899
I’m not talking to you.

481
00:36:35,010 --> 00:36:36,699
He’s the only person I’ll talk to.

482
00:36:40,771 --> 00:36:41,499
Well…

483
00:36:42,084 --> 00:36:43,660
I’ll ask you honestly.

484
00:36:46,484 --> 00:36:48,001
You didn’t do it alone, did you?

485
00:36:55,063 --> 00:36:56,197
Faith.

486
00:37:00,293 --> 00:37:02,100
Everything Nekros did…

487
00:37:04,220 --> 00:37:05,548
I did it all.

488
00:37:08,706 --> 00:37:10,000
Are you proud of me?

489
00:37:10,404 --> 00:37:11,903
You are, aren’t you?

490
00:37:15,928 --> 00:37:17,995
Do you know Asura?

491
00:37:24,080 --> 00:37:29,657
I want to know how you chose
which chapter to imitate,

492
00:37:30,060 --> 00:37:32,247
and when you killed them…

493
00:37:34,010 --> 00:37:35,602
Who helped you come up with the methods?

494
00:37:47,767 --> 00:37:48,699
I…

495
00:37:52,303 --> 00:37:53,899
I’m just a spark of fire.

496
00:37:56,915 --> 00:37:57,900
Floating…

497
00:37:59,225 --> 00:38:00,299
Floating.

498
00:38:02,270 --> 00:38:05,047
Igniting the fire with no doubt.

499
00:38:08,700 --> 00:38:10,368
I’m just the messenger.

500
00:38:17,688 --> 00:38:20,000
A fire that’s started blazing

501
00:38:22,133 --> 00:38:24,001
won’t be so easy to put out.

502
00:38:36,540 --> 00:38:37,247
Let’s go.

503
00:38:37,420 --> 00:38:38,401
Time’s up.

504
00:39:03,560 --> 00:39:04,414
Inspector.

505
00:39:08,030 --> 00:39:09,240
Where are the old files?

506
00:39:09,540 --> 00:39:11,351
I looked for them like you asked me to.

507
00:39:11,887 --> 00:39:12,734
But…

508
00:39:12,761 --> 00:39:13,804
What a coincidence.

509
00:39:14,510 --> 00:39:17,808
Are you also looking for the files
for the Thai Investment Bank case?

510
00:39:18,733 --> 00:39:19,398
Yes.

511
00:39:20,177 --> 00:39:22,503
There’s something
I’d like to cross-reference.

512
00:39:22,680 --> 00:39:25,660
But if you’re working on it,
I’ll have Nop come back for them later.

513
00:39:27,930 --> 00:39:28,746
Inspector.

514
00:39:29,620 --> 00:39:32,303
You need to take better care
of your sister and Mr. Kaye.

515
00:39:34,571 --> 00:39:38,600
I got a report
that Mr. Kaye and your sister

516
00:39:39,020 --> 00:39:41,010
asked to visit Kim in prison today.

517
00:39:42,660 --> 00:39:43,598
And one more thing…

518
00:39:44,026 --> 00:39:48,496
I heard Mr. Kaye was initially
the prime suspect in this case.

519
00:39:50,973 --> 00:39:52,102
I’m worried about you.

520
00:39:52,608 --> 00:39:54,801
I don’t want this to blow up.

521
00:39:55,260 --> 00:39:56,595
The case is closed.

522
00:39:56,922 --> 00:39:58,204
The public is satisfied.

523
00:39:58,539 --> 00:39:59,656
The higher-ups are happy.

524
00:40:01,263 --> 00:40:03,659
Let’s not dig up the mess again.

525
00:40:20,727 --> 00:40:21,902
Praew, listen to me.

526
00:40:22,345 --> 00:40:23,995
We need to tell Phat about this.

527
00:40:25,494 --> 00:40:27,903
But if we do, he’s going to be so mad.

528
00:40:27,967 --> 00:40:29,850
But this is a matter of life and death.

529
00:40:30,023 --> 00:40:33,204
If it’s really Chapter 20,
Phat needs to know.

530
00:40:33,767 --> 00:40:35,850
He’ll stop the murderer in time.
We need to tell him.

531
00:40:38,040 --> 00:40:39,490
Why did you two show up at the prison?

532
00:40:40,167 --> 00:40:41,002
Huh?

533
00:40:41,777 --> 00:40:42,850
Phat, listen.

534
00:40:42,921 --> 00:40:44,497
First of all, I’m sorry.

535
00:40:45,108 --> 00:40:47,357
But I needed to go because
I received some new information.

536
00:40:47,385 --> 00:40:49,200
It got me thinking

537
00:40:50,200 --> 00:40:52,500
that the person who doesn’t want
this nonsense to end…

538
00:40:52,990 --> 00:40:53,897
is you.

539
00:40:56,530 --> 00:40:57,896
You want people to keep dying

540
00:40:58,642 --> 00:41:00,490
as sacrifices for your psychotic manga.

541
00:41:01,890 --> 00:41:02,899
Am I right?

542
00:41:03,084 --> 00:41:03,897
Phat.

543
00:41:04,085 --> 00:41:05,897
We were just looking for the truth.

544
00:41:06,453 --> 00:41:07,930
Don’t take your frustration out on Kaye.

545
00:41:07,951 --> 00:41:09,303
You need to keep quiet.

546
00:41:10,190 --> 00:41:12,090
You’re just his fan.

547
00:41:12,180 --> 00:41:14,102
You’re only too willing to let him
mess with your head

548
00:41:14,499 --> 00:41:16,002
and be used like a tool.

549
00:41:18,136 --> 00:41:21,002
You’re not a cop or a reporter.

550
00:41:21,773 --> 00:41:23,800
What you are is just a brat!

551
00:41:25,802 --> 00:41:26,506
Yeah!

552
00:41:26,598 --> 00:41:29,198
I’m just a useless thing to you.

553
00:41:29,522 --> 00:41:31,490
You don’t believe in me at all.

554
00:41:55,611 --> 00:41:56,601
(Good evening.)

555
00:41:56,800 --> 00:41:58,401
(For our special scoop today,)

556
00:41:58,540 --> 00:42:01,299
(we bring you the story of another person
everyone’s been anticipating.)

557
00:42:01,551 --> 00:42:04,080
(The man who left a bruise on my face.)

558
00:42:04,407 --> 00:42:06,170
(Inspector Yotsaphat Traikanawut.)

559
00:42:06,859 --> 00:42:09,296
(I’m sure many are familiar
with his surname.)

560
00:42:09,669 --> 00:42:12,970
(He’s the nephew
of the famous Commissioner Chaiwat.)

561
00:42:13,580 --> 00:42:17,656
(However, this was also the surname
of Commissioner Praphaphat,)

562
00:42:17,740 --> 00:42:19,490
(the Inspector’s very own father,)

563
00:42:19,630 --> 00:42:23,509
(the cop accused of taking bribes
to destroy the evidence regarding)

564
00:42:23,533 --> 00:42:25,894
(the Thai Investment Bank case,)

565
00:42:26,152 --> 00:42:30,601
(allowing the investors to walk free
while the grassroot people took the blame.)

566
00:42:30,997 --> 00:42:33,663
(The very reason many families
lost everything they had,)

567
00:42:34,460 --> 00:42:37,499
(and chose to end their own lives
to escape their problems.)

568
00:42:47,440 --> 00:42:50,198
(The number you have dialed
cannot be connected at the moment.)

569
00:42:55,510 --> 00:42:58,600
(The number you have dialed
cannot be connected at the moment.)

570
00:43:40,100 --> 00:43:41,598
You knew all this time, didn’t you?

571
00:43:42,244 --> 00:43:46,497
Your father destroyed my family.

572
00:43:49,165 --> 00:43:50,600
You can hate my father.

573
00:43:51,717 --> 00:43:52,902
You can hate me.

574
00:43:54,220 --> 00:43:55,200
I’ll get it.

575
00:43:57,100 --> 00:43:59,702
But I hate what he did
a hundred times more than you do.

576
00:44:04,070 --> 00:44:08,998
But does that hatred bring him back
to life and put him in jail?

577
00:44:10,576 --> 00:44:12,201
Does it make your father better?

578
00:44:17,390 --> 00:44:19,000
When did you know about my father?

579
00:44:21,160 --> 00:44:22,299
Did you stalk me?

580
00:44:45,330 --> 00:44:46,173
Dad.

581
00:44:47,271 --> 00:44:50,299
I’m sorry I’ve been away for so many days.

582
00:44:56,930 --> 00:44:58,044
How are you doing, Dad?

583
00:45:00,675 --> 00:45:01,801
Are you well?

584
00:45:04,748 --> 00:45:06,300
Did you have dinner?

585
00:45:07,710 --> 00:45:09,278
Let’s get you cleaned up, shall we?

586
00:45:13,285 --> 00:45:16,097
I know what you’re trying to hide.

587
00:45:19,060 --> 00:45:20,303
I understand.

588
00:45:26,890 --> 00:45:30,405
Because if I were you,
I wouldn’t be able to put up with it.

589
00:45:36,840 --> 00:45:38,598
The reason I chose to be a cop

590
00:45:40,862 --> 00:45:43,100
was because I wanted to remind myself

591
00:45:43,830 --> 00:45:45,801
that I would never make
the same mistake my father did.

592
00:45:52,401 --> 00:45:53,300
But you…

593
00:45:58,699 --> 00:46:01,002
Did you ever choose to do anything
besides being stuck in the past?

594
00:46:37,710 --> 00:46:39,302
Thank you for coming with me.

595
00:46:41,780 --> 00:46:43,397
Are you sure about this, Praew?

596
00:46:46,180 --> 00:46:46,998
I mean…

597
00:46:48,090 --> 00:46:51,274
I can tell from out here
that they’re not good people.

598
00:46:52,871 --> 00:46:55,920
The police thought this case
was over with Kim.

599
00:46:56,900 --> 00:47:00,896
But if we gather information
and prove that it’s not over…

600
00:47:01,560 --> 00:47:03,160
I think it’s worth the risk.

601
00:47:04,955 --> 00:47:05,699
Let’s do it.

602
00:47:07,490 --> 00:47:08,297
Let’s go.

603
00:47:31,660 --> 00:47:32,687
First of all,

604
00:47:33,390 --> 00:47:34,804
you need to stop being scared.

605
00:47:35,660 --> 00:47:37,201
Let your body navigate the flow.

606
00:47:38,770 --> 00:47:39,970
When the opponent has an opening,

607
00:47:41,411 --> 00:47:43,100
elbow him with everything you have.

608
00:47:43,894 --> 00:47:45,102
See clearly.

609
00:47:46,284 --> 00:47:47,660
Don’t look away.

610
00:47:48,379 --> 00:47:49,660
If you do,

611
00:47:50,364 --> 00:47:51,657
you won’t see your enemy.

612
00:47:54,250 --> 00:47:56,103
Focus on the opponent in front of you.

613
00:47:56,760 --> 00:47:57,654
Twist your hips.

614
00:48:05,388 --> 00:48:10,400
The number 20 Kim wrote on the glass
must be the clue for the next victim.

615
00:48:11,070 --> 00:48:13,640
There’s a type of murderer
called Mastermind.

616
00:48:13,684 --> 00:48:14,530
He controls everything.

617
00:48:16,417 --> 00:48:17,102
Praew!

618
00:48:17,930 --> 00:48:19,562
I understand what it feels like
for a big brother

619
00:48:19,590 --> 00:48:21,998
to be powerless in saving his sister.

620
00:48:22,280 --> 00:48:24,299
You’re doing your best as a brother.

621
00:48:24,391 --> 00:48:27,670
Your visit that day was the last words
he needed before he killed himself

622
00:48:27,700 --> 00:48:28,980
and erased all traces back to you.

623
00:48:29,100 --> 00:48:30,604
Every cop in the world would think that.

624
00:48:30,915 --> 00:48:31,868
What about you?

625
00:48:32,619 --> 00:48:33,970
Do you still think I’m the murderer?
